<title>ITALY: SniaBPD 1H96 cons pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>SniaBPD 1H96 cons pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30, 1996. (In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		    72.7  vs     59</p>
<p>    Cons net turnover		  1,604.7  (up 3.6 pct)</p>
<p>    Cons operating result		 94.4  vs     90.2</p>
<p>    Net financial debt		   478    (up 84 bln)</p>
<p>    Investments			    102.7  (up 28.4 pct)</p>
<p>    Extraordinary income		   5.5</p>
<p>    Parent pretax profit		  31.5  vs     22</p>
<p>Note - Snia Bpd, which is part of the Fiat group, said net financial debt grew from the level given at the end of December 1995 on account of acquisitions made in the period.</p>
<p>Snia said the unfavourable forecasts for economic conditions in the second half of the year meant it was possible the group would show a slightly lower result in all of 1996 compared with 1995.--Milan bureau +392 66129507</p>
</text>
